d the requirement that the whole string matches (a trailing `\\n` must not match).\n- **Field names:** dotted, hyphenated and `[key]` names, nested dictionaries, telling apart names that turn into the same internal group name (`a.b` and `a_b`), repeated names (including the `RepeatedNameError` when their types differ), and that `named_fields`/`fixed_fields` return copies.\n- **Numbers:** `d` with automatic `0x`/`0b`/`0o` prefixes, signs, width, zero-padding, `,`/`_` separators and `<`/`>`/`^`/`=` alignment; `b`/`o`/`x`/`X`/`n`; `f`/`F` (including `.0f`, `nan`, `inf` and the `Decimal` return type); `e`/`g`/`%`; and `int_convert` tested directly.\n- **Text types:** `w W s S D l`, width, precision, fill characters (including regex special ones) and alignment.\n- **Dates and times:** all `t*` types (`ti te tg ta th tc tt ts`) including AM/PM and the 12 o'clock edge cases, timezone offsets in several styles, `date_convert` called directly, strftime-style `%` formats, and `FixedTzOffset`.\n- **Spans:** checked after types that add extra internal regex groups, so a wrong group count shows up as a wrong position.\n- **Other:** custom types via `extra_types`/`with_pattern` (including `regex_group_count`), `search`/`findall` with `pos`/`endpos`/`evaluate_result=False`, the `repr`s of `Parser`, `Result` and `FixedTzOffset`, and round trips through `str.format`.\n\nMy first run had 14 failures. All were mistakes in my expectations, not library bugs, so I changed the tests to match what the code actually does:\n- **Width is a minimum length for the captured text,** so `{:>4}` on `\"  ab\"` captures `\"  ab\"` with the spaces.\n- **`{:d}` accepts a leading space as the sign,** so `search` reports the match as starting one character earlier than you might expect.\n- **`fixed_fields` holds internal regex group numbers,** not positions in the result.\n- **`date_convert` ignores `mm=0`,** because 0 counts as false in `if mm and dd`; I used non-zero group numbers in that test.\n\nOne 